{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "50971cdf-e1a0-8b12-b654-2763b14ef70c",
  "created_at": "2026-01-13T12:39:00-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, City Clerk",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Terrence Quinn",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Owen Haskell",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:36:34-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City Clerk's office, Owen Haskell speaking. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:36:38-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, hello. [pause] I'm trying to reach the, um, the tax division. The state tax division. Is this them?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:36:44-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, sir, this is the City Clerk's office in Newport. The state tax division is a different office. It's run by the state, not the city."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:36:52-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. [pause] Newport. Well, that's not what I wanted. I thought I had the number out of the book. I've got the paper right here somewhere."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:00-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's all right, take your time. Do you have the number in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:05-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do. It starts with, um, four oh one. Isn't that the state? I always thought four oh one was the whole state of Rhode Island."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:13-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is, sir, the four oh one covers the whole state. So that part's right. But both the city and the state offices use it, so the area code alone won't tell you which office you've reached."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:24-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hm. [pause] So it's the same area code but a different office. I don't follow that. I thought the numbers went to one place."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:32-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I know it's confusing. The area code is just the region. The seven digits after it are what pick the office. So you may have one digit off, or you may have written down the city's line by mistake."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:44-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Could be. I wrote it on the back of an envelope. My grandson, no, my, um, my daughter's boy... she had him on the phone with me, and the school called, you see. He lost his jacket again. The third one. So I wrote the number in a hurry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:37:58-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ah, well, that would do it, writing it down in the middle of all that. Kids and jackets, they go together."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:05-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. [pause] Now where was I. The tax people. So you're not them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:10-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Correct, I'm not. What I'd suggest is looking up the Rhode Island Division of Taxation. You can find it by calling directory assistance, or the phone book should list the state government pages in the blue section."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:21-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The blue pages. I have those, I think. Under R, for Rhode Island?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:26-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It might be under R, or it might be under State Government. If it's not under R, try the other one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:33-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "State Government. Alright. [pause] And do I put the four oh one first or not, if I'm at home here?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Whatever the book shows, dial all of it, area code included. That's the safest way."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:44-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "All of it. Alright. I'm sorry to have bothered you, young man. I'm still not sure I understand about the four oh one, but I'll try the book."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:53-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No bother at all, sir. Good luck with it, and you take care."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-13T12:38:58-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. Goodbye now."
    }
  ],
